# klip-dictionary-data v6 — provenance manifest
#
# Every number here is measured, not carried over. One block per language.
#
# **ALL NINETEEN PACKS ARE ATTACHED.** v5 held twelve back above a 60 MiB
# line. That line is now a **Wi-Fi GATE, NOT A SHIPPING GATE** (owner ruling
# 2026-11-06): every pack publishes, every download defaults to Wi-Fi, and a
# pack over 60 MiB additionally shows its size in the app's confirm step
# before anything starts. Nothing under 60 MiB needs the extra confirm.
#
#   NO EXTRA CONFIRM (<=60 MiB)  da el hi ko nl no zh
#   SIZE SHOWN IN CONFIRM        ar de en es fr it ja pl pt ru sv tr
#
# BUILDER      Klip commit 337889669ca0ce079e2c4fba869afea866b36fd6
#              tool/dict_pack/build_pack.dart
# EXPORTER     export_pack.py in this repo, python3 -I, stdlib only.
#
# ── WHAT CHANGED IN THE PACKS: THE FORM TABLE COLLAPSED ──────────────────
#
# The form table is where the bytes were. Turkish carried 2,817,353 form rows
# for 40,251 entries; Spanish 1,882,928; English 1,371,024; Arabic 3,067,177
# for 229,902 entries, because its conjugation tables are exhaustive AND every
# vocalisation variant of one written form folds to the same key.
#
# v6 collapses the form table on **(fold, target)**:
#
#   KEY        fold + target. Two spellings that fold alike but point at
#              DIFFERENT lemmas keep TWO rows, so no lemma pointer can be
#              lost. That is a property of the key, not of the data.
#   TAGS       the UNION is kept across collapsed rows, never one chosen
#              arbitrarily — a tag set is a grammatical reading.
#   SPELLING   the FIRST IN SOURCE ORDER is kept, and the new `collapsed`
#              column records how many rows merged, so the loss is visible.
#              Acceptable because the form index matches on the FOLD: a
#              lookup never needed the discarded spellings to succeed.
#
# **`pack_format` IS STILL 2, AND THAT WAS CHECKED RATHER THAN ASSUMED.**
# `collapsed` is additive and no query reads it; the app's form queries name
# their columns, so a v6 pack opens unchanged in a build that predates it.
# Bumping would have made every v6 pack unopenable until an app release
# caught up — the data/app coupling that publishing finished packs exists to
# avoid.
#
# ── EVERY EXTRACT RE-VERIFIED; EVERY PACK HASHED BEFORE ANY DELETION ─────
#
# All 19 extract.sha256 were recomputed and matched the value v4 recorded.
# Each pack was hashed as soon as it existed. `pack.sha256` carries a real
# digest for all nineteen; none is unrecorded.
#

